{#
  ABOUT ME — Figma 185:2029. Content from _data/about.js.

  TWO COLUMNS of equal width inside the same 120px gutters as the header and
  hero, so the page frame runs unbroken down the page. The rules are part of
  that frame: the outer pair continue the header's, and the comp adds two more
  inside — a divider between the columns and one above the time widget.

  THE TIME WIDGET IS STATIC. Every value is mocked from the comp. The
  data-clock-* hooks are the contract for the later phase that makes it live:
  scripts/clock.js already computes exactly these three fields, so that phase
  is a rewire, not a rewrite. Do not rename them casually.
#}

<section class="about" id="about-me" data-header-theme="light">
  <div class="about__inner">
    <div class="about__figure-col">
      {#
        TWO LAYERS, frame behind the figure — the same order Figma draws them.
        The frame is an exported open path (see about.js); the figure is a
        transparent PNG that overhangs it at the bottom, so the arms read as
        crossing the line rather than sitting inside a box.
      #}
      <div class="about__figure">
        <img
          class="about__frame"
          src="{{ about.illustration.frame }}"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          draggable="false"
        />
        <img
          class="about__illustration"
          src="{{ about.illustration.file }}"
          alt="{{ about.illustration.alt }}"
          draggable="false"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="about__body">
      <div class="about__content">
        <h2 class="about__heading">
          <span class="about__heading-lead">{{ about.heading.lead }}</span>
          <span class="about__heading-rest">{{ about.heading.rest }}</span>
        </h2>

        {#
          NO STATS ROW, NO LOCATION LINE. 543:1124 has neither: the column is
          heading -> three paragraphs -> clock band. The country moved into the
          third paragraph as bold text, which is why the flag <img> went too.

          RUNS, NOT A STRING. about.bio is a list of lists now, so the emphasis
          the node specifies lives in the data. The whitespace control is
          load-bearing: the runs carry their own spaces and must be joined with
          nothing between them.
        #}
        {%- for para in about.bio %}
          <p class="about__bio">
            {%- for run in para -%}
              {%- if run.bold %}<strong>{{ run.text }}</strong>{% else %}{{ run.text }}{% endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </p>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      {#
        A ROW, NOT A STACK — 543:1139. The clock box (118x80, at x=32) sits left
        of the status block (429x44, at x=174), the 24px between them being the
        gap. Both are centred on the band's middle.

        THE CLOCK IS FACELESS, and that is the node, not an omission: 543:1181
        draws a hub dot and thin hands with NO circle, and the digital time sits
        over them. Do not add a ring to "finish" it.

        THREE HANDS, AND THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. 543:1181 draws a short
        thick grey hour hand, a longer thick grey minute hand, and a long THIN
        BLACK second hand — the lengths and weights are what tell them apart when
        there is no face to read them against, so the classes carry them.

        THE HANDS ARE LIVE, BY TWO DIFFERENT MEANS. Hour and minute are rotated
        by scripts/clock.js on its existing 60s tick; the second hand sweeps in
        CSS instead, because a per-second JS tick to move one line is a timer the
        page does not otherwise need. The <line>s point at 12 as authored. The
        pivot (52 30) is repeated in clock.js and in _about.css's
        transform-origin — all three must agree.
      #}
      <div class="about__clock" data-clock>
        <div class="about__clock-face">
          <svg
            class="about__clock-hands"
            viewBox="0 0 118 80"
            fill="none"
            aria-hidden="true"
            focusable="false"
          >
            <line class="about__clock-hand about__clock-hand--hour" data-clock-hour
                  x1="52" y1="30" x2="52" y2="12" />
            <line class="about__clock-hand about__clock-hand--minute" data-clock-minute
                  x1="52" y1="30" x2="52" y2="2" />
            <line class="about__clock-hand about__clock-hand--second" data-clock-second
                  x1="52" y1="30" x2="52" y2="-6" />
            <circle class="about__clock-hub" cx="52" cy="30" r="3.5" />
          </svg>
          <p class="about__clock-time">
            <span class="about__clock-value" data-clock-time>{{ about.clock.time }}</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about__clock-body">
        <p class="about__clock-status">
          {#
            NOT IN THE COMP. Figma 185:2029 draws no indicator — the v2 sidebar
            widget had one at the tip of an L-connector and the brief asks for
            it back, so it is added here rather than invented silently. It is
            one span and one CSS block; delete both to return to the comp.
          #}
          <span class="about__clock-dot" data-clock-dot aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="about__clock-lead" data-clock-lead>{{ about.clock.statusLead }}</span>
          <span class="about__clock-headline" data-clock-status>{{ about.clock.status }}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="about__clock-detail" data-clock-detail>{{ about.clock.detail }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
